+
+## Authority and provenance
+
+Controlling matrix: `docs/v2-completion-plan/v2.14 — Authoritative IM-01–IM-14 Execution Matrix.md` §14E, October 18 reviewer acceptance of IM-13. Supplied IM-14 work order authorizes documentation reconciliation but forbids self-approval, product/catalog changes or final v2 declaration. Completion Contract, P4, approved P5, Architecture Resolutions, five historical questions, closure backlog and Decisions048/051/052 remain source authorities. `protected-before.json` records their bytes at the actual starting checkout.
+
+Original RTF authority is retained; `recovered/Approved v2 2B-P5.txt`, `recovered/v2 Architectural Resolutions.txt` and `recovered/V2 Execution Matrix.txt` are plain-text inspection extracts, not replacement approvals. Original Admin Guide and prior external record-level audit were not found; no inaccessible source is claimed inspected. The actual eight repository philosophy task bullets are mapped without claiming identity with a lost archival original. See SOURCE-* ledger entries and authorized substitute rationale.
+
+`report-inspection-index.md` provides exact report section/line references; `report-reconciliation-extracts.md` preserves the relevant acceptance/limits crosswalk from each complete report. Individual package acceptance authority is the current matrix plus each dated closure entry/report; a date is not fabricated when only execution date is known.
+
+## Final accepted runtime proof — IM-13, not an IM-14 full rerun
+
+Use `../im13/closure/inputs-before.json`, `inputs-after.json`, `binding-result.json`, `commands.json`, `distribution-hashes.json`, `http-release.json`, `http-negative-controls.json`, `missing-schema-control.json`, `browser-result.json`, `browser-probe-after.json`, `packaged-http.json`, `editor-workflow.json` and `final-consistency.json` under that same directory.
+
+The original interrupted report, intermediate integrity FAIL, original incomplete65-response HTTP claim and first closure Node26/jsdom failure are retained. Only the final corrected decide schema and fresh 402-input binding supersede those two verification gaps. Final22 commands exited 0, with 631 backend tests,162 frontend tests/23 files,16 Python, six validators, real Docker,65 exact HTTP checks/four SPA-media paths and scoped seven-journey browser/manual evidence. Remote AI success was not exercised.
+
+IM-14 `inspection-checks.json` independently matches all 402 current inputs and all 22 log hashes/exits to those accepted artifacts. There is no excuse to treat a historical failed run as PASS, and no need to rerun the complete release suite for documentation-only additions.
+
+## Narrow IM-14 checks and change protection
+
+`document-command-ledger.json` records exact command argument arrays, actual temporary candidate working directories, exits, UTC timestamps and output hashes. It covers real validator help, packaged expiry help, six validators against an isolated reconstructed full catalog and a targeted supplementary schema invocation. `recovery-check.json` records copied/source catalog hash equality and limited scope; this is not a production restore test.
+
+The targeted schema actually passes 171/171 with warnings. `initial-command-checks/` retains the first outer checker assertion that incorrectly expected failure; the validator itself exited 0. The draft interpretation and expected exit were corrected without changing source/catalog/validator code. Passing optional-fact structure is not proof of provider truth or complete authoring.
+
+`document-checks.json` covers final Markdown links, ledger references/IDs/statuses and source/evidence completeness. `starting-state.json`, `ending-state.json`, `protection-result.json` and `artifact-manifest.json` identify actual HEAD, original 1526 protected paths, exact new files and hashes. `documentation.patch` records the new core-document content; the manifest covers generated ledger/logs/extracts separately. Production code is untouched, so no code mirror synchronization was necessary.
+
+## Reviewer gate and continuing limits
+
+Proposed IM-14 outcome: Satisfied / v2 eligible for reviewer closure, conditioned on reviewer acceptance of the complete evidence and approved manual/substitute boundaries. No required-v2/evidence-needed row is unresolved in the ledger. IM-14 itself remains pending reviewer decision; authority/matrix status was not changed.
+
+NOT TESTED: comprehensive WCAG certification, physical devices, screen-reader execution, exhaustive external source/provider/RSS correctness and successful remote AI responses. Actual production-host security/TLS/backup recovery is not certified by local evidence. Source freshness and substantive accuracy remain ongoing human duties. Empty admitted local Law cache is not absence of relevant Delaware laws. Future HOST graphs, Admin workflows, second launch and library design remain explicit later scope, not done capabilities.
